.TH BSKYTEST 1
.SH NAME
bskytest \- test bsky(1)'s decoders and network paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bskytest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Bskytest
calls
.IR bsky (1)'s
own in-process test seams, needing no credentials file and no
network mocking. Offline seams run first, decoding hand-built JSON
fixtures in each endpoint's real response shape, so a network outage
fails late with the live legs named instead of masking decoder
regressions:
.TP
.B feedtest
the timeline walk: missing post/author/record fallbacks, the
newest-first ordering, the
.B -v
uri/cid lines, and cursor extraction;
.TP
.B notiftest
the notifications walk (the one endpoint with no possible
unauthenticated live leg);
.TP
.B threadtest
a hand-built nested thread: two ancestors, nested replies, and an
unavailable node;
.TP
.B profiletest
the profile fields and counts;
.TP
.B buildtest
the createRecord bodies \(em post, reply (with root/parent refs),
like, follow \(em pinned byte for byte, plus URL percent-encoding.
.PP
The live seams then hit real endpoints:
.TP
.B pubtest
a public profile fetch by hostname;
.TP
.B resolvetest
handle-to-DID resolution, the same path
.B follow
uses;
.TP
.B livethreadtest
a real thread (bsky.app's newest post) through the same
.B threaddecode
the offline seam pinned;
.TP
.B postpubtest
a deliberately bogus login, which must draw the server's own decoded
.B AuthenticationRequired
(or, when repeated runs have tripped the limiter,
.BR RateLimitExceeded )
\(em proof the POSTed JSON body arrived intact;
.TP
.B authposttest
a createRecord with a bogus token, which must draw a decoded server
error through the full authenticated-POST path without ever writing
anything to a real account.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/bskytest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR bsky (1),
.IR mastotest (1),
.IR httpstest (1),
.IR https (2)
.SH BUGS
The live legs need the real network and real third-party servers; a
failure there can mean the world changed rather than the code.
Nothing here (deliberately) publishes a post, so the server's final
acceptance of a well-formed createRecord is not exercised \(em see
.IR bsky (1)'s
own BUGS.
